{"school":{"dbn":"24Q088","name":"P.S. 88 Seneca","boro":"Queens","district":"24","district_label":"District 24","report_type":"EMS","report_types":"EMS","school_type":"Elementary","grades":"3K-5","status":"open","enrollment":694,"enrollment_year":"2024-25","address":"60-85 CATALPA AVENUE, QUEENS, NY 11385","phone":"718-821-8121","website":"https://www.ps88q.com/","directory_url":"https://www.myschools.nyc/en/schools/3k/62861","accessibility":"Partially Accessible","overview":"PS 88Q's Early Childhood Program is designed to provide a nurturing and enriching environment that supports the development of young learners through authentic early childhood education. Our program emphasizes the importance of early literacy skills, offering children the tools they need to develop a strong foundation for reading and writing. We value the diversity of our community and provide access to multiple languages, ensuring that all students feel included and have the opportunity to develop bilingual or multilingual skills.Our approach is rooted in play-based learning, where children explore, discover, and make sense of the world around them in a hands-on and engaging way. \nWe believe that strong partnerships with families are essential for the success of our students, and we actively work to involve parents and caregivers in their child's learning journey.In addition to a supportive learning environment, PS 88Q provides access to valuable community resources Children who live in NYC are eligible to begin 3-K during the fall of the calendar year they turn 3. There are different types of seats available in 3-K programs; some programs may offer more than one seat type, and you can list them separately on your application. For more information, please click on the options listed below or visit nyc.gov/3K. Each early childhood setting offers key health supports. District schools and Pre-K Centers have full-time nurses on site. Please contact EarlyChildhoodHealth@schools.nyc.gov with any q